{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1630 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "b0dfd983a5dfb940aafe8f5434623c72223605d518dffdff222ce30aadfaea15" :edb/db-before-t 1629 :edb/db-after-t 1630 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534942 50 #inst "2026-10-08T11:38:29.510Z" 13194139534942 true] [17592186059680 1020 #edb/ref 17592186321373 13194139534942 true] [17592186059681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186321377 13194139534942 true] [17592186321373 1017 #edb/ref 17592186321374 13194139534942 true] [17592186321373 1089 "q-275757" 13194139534942 true] [17592186321373 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534942 true] [17592186321373 1100 "The entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & -2\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $-1.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" 13194139534942 true] [17592186321373 1113 #uuid "f1605a7c-6610-56ff-a112-240e6e5bbd01" 13194139534942 true] [17592186321373 1145 "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & -2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ k & -2\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2+k)-(-4+2)-(2k+2) \\\\  & =2+k+2-2k-2 \\\\  & =2-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}^{t}={c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-k}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{k-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{13}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{k-2} & =-1 \\\\ -1\\cdot (k-2) & =2 \\\\ k-2 & =-2 \\\\ k & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534942 true] [17592186321374 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321375 13194139534942 true] [17592186321374 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321376 13194139534942 true] [17592186321374 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534942 true] [17592186321374 1041 "field-1" 13194139534942 true] [17592186321374 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321376 13194139534942 true] [17592186321374 1110 #uuid "abc3316d-4bab-54f5-aa83-c84a92afd041" 13194139534942 true] [17592186321375 1034 "1" 13194139534942 true] [17592186321375 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534942 true] [17592186321375 1111 #uuid "392b40d0-742a-5201-9772-387ceac68044" 13194139534942 true] [17592186321376 1034 "0" 13194139534942 true] [17592186321376 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534942 true] [17592186321376 1111 #uuid "5fab8c5b-110a-5f53-b3c9-4fd77954da68" 13194139534942 true] [17592186321377 1017 #edb/ref 17592186321378 13194139534942 true] [17592186321377 1089 "q-319409" 13194139534942 true] [17592186321377 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534942 true] [17592186321377 1100 "Determine the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n${a}_{32}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534942 true] [17592186321377 1113 #uuid "3e46c518-3e5c-53ed-8495-f09dea2fdfbf" 13194139534942 true] [17592186321377 1145 "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(6-0)-0(-3-0)-1(1-0) \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}^{t}={c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2-0) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{11}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534942 true] [17592186321378 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321379 13194139534942 true] [17592186321378 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534942 true] [17592186321378 1041 "field-1" 13194139534942 true] [17592186321378 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321379 13194139534942 true] [17592186321378 1110 #uuid "50ec604c-1d1b-5e6c-8052-8a4b3e24aec1" 13194139534942 true] [17592186321379 1034 "-\\frac{2}{11}" 13194139534942 true] [17592186321379 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534942 true] [17592186321379 1111 #uuid "f9092226-c93b-564e-8674-90cdda0e56fc" 13194139534942 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-275757" 17592186321373 "q-275757/field-1" 17592186321374 "q-275757/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" 17592186321375 "q-275757/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" 17592186321376 "q-319409" 17592186321377 "q-319409/field-1" 17592186321378 "q-319409/field-1/fd9e7a740343f6f85c50219552c3c4e2bc9558e9c34cb9f4697cfbd10f2c3da0" 17592186321379}}
